{
 "_doc": "Tier-2 wilderness set piece for random worlds (site forest): what the player's own base could become, and how it fell. A scrap-and-log palisade (w3_scrap_palisade sections facing out, the chained gate on the lane with TURN BACK over it, stake rows) closes a yard of raised beds, rain catchers, two watch platforms, a coop, a smokehouse and the well; the house (kit rooms, white siding, every window boarded) has a root-cellar bunker cut into the terrain under it, reached down a stair from the kitchen, its steel door deadbolted, with a ladder up through a hatch into the cellar-entry lean-to whose outside door is bolted: the shortcut. Route: the lane -> the chained gate -> round the wall to where it was broken through (jaws in the gap; Ray's axe) -> the yard -> the house's back door, kicked in, cans strung across it (they wake the house) -> the kitchen: Della's calendar, the bunker key on its hook -> down to the cellar -> the bunker's steel door (opening it wakes the family; Tom, guardian) -> the stores -> up the ladder into the lean-to -> draw its bolt. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
