   "author": "Hollowmere team (agent X)",
   "story": "The Haldanes held their homestead for fourteen months. Ray and his son Tom pulled the tin off the barn and the doors off the cars and walled the yard with them; Della planted the raised beds and set the rain barrels; old Pop took the north platform at night, and every evening somebody strung the cans. They boarded the windows, dug the root cellar out into a bunker with a steel door and a bolt-hole up through the lean-to, and practised getting into it. They came through three Hums. On the seventh night of the fourteenth month something big came at the east wall where the ground was soft. Ray held the gap with the axe while the others got down the hole. Tom bolted the bunker from inside, left the key on the hook by his mother's calendar for whoever came for them from up top, and wrote that Pop had a fever, and so did he.",
